As an East Coaster, I wanted to make sure I understand how the time
change affects the start of the DevNull tournament this weekend.

Here's how I understand it:

At 2am on November 1st, those of us who observe daylight savings time
will be setting our clocks back to 1am.

The tournament begins at 12am (Nov 1st) in the PACIFIC time zone.  The
ending of daylight savings will not affect the start of the tourney,
but we will get an extra hour in the first day of the tournament.
This is a very simple situation for those in California and the West
Coast.

For those of us on the East Coast, it is a bit more complicated.  We
will have ALREADY set our clocks back at 2am (which was 11pm in the
Pacific time zone).  When the tournament starts an hour later, we will
be hitting 2am AGAIN.

So for each time zone:
Pacific - 12am
Mountain - 1am (before time change)
Central - 1am (after time change)
Eastern - 2am (after time change)

